    "model": {
      "unigram": "P1(w) = (1 - p_oov) * count(w) / (sum of vocabulary counts)",
      "unknown": "P_unk(w) = p_oov * P_len(|w|) * prod_i P_letter(w_i) with P_letter = order-1 letter model; p_oov and P_len (add-0.5 smoothed, lengths 1..30, geometric 0.8 tail) measured on the Gutenberg corpus tokens missing from the vocabulary. This is a proper distribution over all strings and penalises an unknown word by about 1.258 log10 units per letter on average (the letter entropy) plus the OOV overhead log10 p_oov + log10 P_len, so known words win whenever they explain the text.",
      "bigram": "P(w2|w1) = lam * c2(w1 w2)/c1(w1) + (1 - lam * s(w1)) * P(w2), s(w1) = sum over listed bigrams of c2(w1 .)/c1(w1), c1(<S>) = N sentences; lam tuned on held-out Gutenberg word pairs",
